# Keep the build context small — only what the Dockerfile actually copies stays in.

# Deps are freshly installed in the image (npm ci)
node_modules
renderer/node_modules
renderer/dist

# RUNTIME STATE WITH CREDENTIALS IN IT — never in a build context.
#
# `config` is the host side of the /config volume, and in a standard checkout it
# is a subdirectory of this one: the shipped compose file mounts `./config`. It
# holds every configured user's POESESSID and account name
# (networth-users.json) and the admin password (admin-password). The Dockerfile
# copies none of it — but the build context is everything that is SENT to the
# docker daemon, so without this line every `docker compose up -d --build` hands
# those secrets over, and a later COPY that reaches wider than it meant to would
# put them in the image. Measured against docker, not assumed: with no line
# matching it, a file under config/ arrives in the context.
#
# `config.host-update` is deploy/host-update.sh's own directory (WORK_DIR), a
# sibling of the config directory and therefore in the checkout as well. Its
# staging files hold the RAW build output — the redaction that takes credentials
# out of a failing `git`'s remote URL happens later, in the server.
#
# The script refuses to run when the build context does not exclude these two.
config
config.host-update

# The other secret shapes .gitignore keeps out of the repository. None of them
# is copied into the image either, and none of them has business being sent to
# the daemon. docker-compose.override.yml is per-machine and is where an
# operator's environment (and its secrets) ends up.
.env
.env.*
config.toml
*.secret
docker-compose.override.yml

# VCS / Editor / OS
.git
.gitignore
.superpowers
.DS_Store
*.log

# Not needed in the image
docs
daemon
systemd
# The update button's host half: it runs on the docker host, where the checkout
# and the docker daemon are. Shipping it inside the container would only make
# it look like it belonged there.
deploy

# Build artefacts — regenerated in the image
backend/v2/*.bundle.mjs
renderer/public/data/**/*.index.bin

# Internal reports / notes
**/*-report.md
**/PROTOCOL.md

# Market fixtures: the raw snapshots (local only) and the tracked cut the
# tests read. Neither is part of the image.
backend/v2/fixtures/
